# Thin Shell — Host-probe Playwright E2E

Phase **4by** adds an **opt-in** Playwright suite for `GET /workspace-host-probe?pluginId=…`.

Unit contracts (TS-4S-01…06) remain the default gate. Browser E2E is **not** wired into CI full gates or `pre-commit:fast`.

## Why opt-in

Starting Next + API for Playwright is multi-minute and needs Postgres / host DNS (`*.localhost`). Thin-shell DoD does not require that loop on every commit.

## Route contract (browser)

| Request | Expected `data-testid` |
| --- | --- |
| `/workspace-host-probe` (no `pluginId`) | `workspace-host-probe-missing-id` |
| `?pluginId=acme` | `workspace-host-probe` + `workspace-host-probe-plugin-id` |
| `?pluginId=denali` | `workspace-host-probe-capability-missing` |
| `?pluginId=no-such-workspace-plugin` | `workspace-host-probe-not-found` |

The route is **public** (not owner-panel protected). Use an operator-capable host (e.g. `denali.localhost`) so middleware host gates pass.

## Run

```bash
# Terminal A — Next already running (example)
cd apps/web && pnpm exec next dev --port 3000 --hostname 127.0.0.1

# Terminal B — browser suite (explicit opt-in)
cd apps/web
HOST_PROBE_E2E=1 \
PW_EXTERNAL_SERVERS=1 \
HOST_PROBE_BASE_URL=http://denali.localhost:3000 \
  pnpm run test:e2e:host-probe
```

| Env | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `HOST_PROBE_E2E=1` | Required — suite skips entirely otherwise |
| `PW_EXTERNAL_SERVERS=1` | Required — no embedded webServer in this config |
| `HOST_PROBE_BASE_URL` | Base URL (default `http://denali.localhost:3000`) |

